      </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="col-lg-8">
      <p>
        E-Learning, or electronic learning, has transformed the way education is delivered and received.
        Its roots trace back to the 1960s with early computer-based training programs.
        During the 1990s, the rise of the internet brought online education to a global audience,
        making learning more flexible and accessible.
        In the 2000s, universities and institutions began offering full online courses and degrees,
        supported by Learning Management Systems (LMS) such as Moodle and Blackboard.
        The 2010s saw the emergence of Massive Open Online Courses (MOOCs) from platforms like Coursera, edX, and Udemy,
        allowing millions of learners worldwide to access quality education.
      </p>
    </div>
